{"text": "School of Law\n\nGOLDEN GATE UNIVERSITY\n\nFall 2008\nTORTS 1 (Law 720A)\nSYLLABUS\n\nProfessor William T. Gallagher\nContact Information:\nOffice: 536 Mission Street, Room 3305\nOffice Hours: T.B.A. AND by Appointment\nOffice Phone: (415) 369-5339\n\nE-Mail: wgallagher@ggu.edu\n\nREQUIRED TEXTS:\n\nProsser, Wade, Schwartz, Kelly and Partlett, Torts: Cases and Materials, | 1\" Edition\n(Foundation Press, 2005) (\u201cCB\u201d)\n\nJohn L. Diamond, Lawrence C. Levine, and M. Stuart Madden, Understanding Torts, 3d\nEd. (LexisNexis 2007) (\u201cUT\u201d)\n\nGGU CYBERCAMPUS NOTICE:\n\nThis class will have a GGU CyberCampus website http://ggucybercampus.org .\nThis site will contain the official syllabus\u2014including any changes or amendments, as\nwell as any official class announcements. Various class handouts will also be made\navailable on this site, including the First Class Assignment, which is to be read before our\ninitial class meeting. Students are expected to access this site regularly to keep apprised\nof course developments.\n\nCOURSE REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. Exam and Grading: There will be a one-hour \u201cclosed-book\u201d midterm exam for\nthis course on October 11, which will constitute 25% of the final course grade. There\nwill also be a three-hour \u201cclosed-book\u201d final exam for this course, which will constitute\n75% of the final course grade. The final exam will be on December 11 6:30PM. Final\ncourse grades may be subject to adjustment based on the policies expressed in the\nattached Memorandum Re Class Attendance, Preparedness, and Participation.\n\n2. Written \u201cProblems\u201d: Students will be required to submit up to 7 brief written\nresponses to posted course \u201cproblems\u201d that require you to apply your growing knowledge\nof tort law to specific issues. These problems will be posted to the class CyberCampus",
